      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A key to the success of chimeric antigen receptor (CAR) T-cell based therapies greatly rely on the capacity to identify and target antigens with expression restrained to tumor cells. Here we present a strategy to generate CAR T-cells that are only effective locally (tumor tissue), potentially also increasing the choice of targetable antigens. By fusing an oxygen sensitive subdomain of HIF1α to a CAR scaffold, we generated CAR T-cells that are responsive to a hypoxic environment, a hallmark of certain tumors. Along with the development of oxygen-sensitive CAR T-cells, this work also provides a basic framework to use a multi-chain CAR as a platform to create the next generation of smarter self-decision making CAR T-cells."},
